Sval: SessionStore saves no window marked unsaved

A window whose custom value "sval-unsaved" is set (setCustomWindowValue) is
left out of the session state SessionStore writes, which a restart, a crash
and Restore Previous Session bring back, and out of the recently closed
windows. Sval marks the windows a WebDriver client opens: their tabs live on a
tree in memory, and a window restored from a record of one would start on
the user's synced document and file the automation's tabs there. No chrome
API keeps a normal window out of the session: SessionStore leaves out only
private windows and taskbar tabs, and closing a restored one at launch
cannot reach Restore Previous Session, which restores into a window already
started.

